# The electric gripper (gripper.tool: a 7th stmbl drive, gripper.conf) in a
# pick-and-place cycle. Closing on the 30 mm part: the fingers stop on it
# (lag > 1 mm: contact), width measured, GRIPPED; the detector's model takes
# the expected 2 kg at once, muted 0.3 s. The payload is checked on the
# lift (standing still, J2's stiction carries most of the new weight): the
# least-squares mass over the moving joints (here J3; J2 creeps under
# v_min) reads 2.8 kg with the perturbed model, 2.3 with the exact one - a
# constant offset, the model's residual floor on this motion: ok (1 kg). Carried, placed, released: the model
# drops it at once (unchecked). No collision
# hit, no fault anywhere.
@program arm/arm_sim
@args arm/arcmate/arcmate_gripper.arm
@include arm/tests/inc_grip_pick.txt
grip expect 30 2.0 0 0 0.15
grip close
run 1.5
tlmove 1.0 799.3 0 1370.9 0 0 0
run 1.2
print grip
tmove 2.0 30 10 10 0 -80 0
run 2.2
print grip
tmove 2.0 30 0 0 0 -90 0
run 2.2
grip open
run 1.5
print grip
tmove 1.5 30 10 10 0 -80 0
run 1.7
print grip coll off hits
@expect arm.grip_state[1] == 2
@expect arm.grip_width[1] > 29.5
@expect arm.grip_width[1] < 30.2
@expect arm.grip_force[1] > 150
@expect arm.pay_state[1] == 3
@expect arm.pay_meas[1] > 1.5
@expect arm.pay_meas[1] < 3.0
@expect arm.pay_model[1] == 2
@expect arm.part_z[1] > 1515
@expect arm.part_z[2] < 1200
@expect arm.grip_held[2] == 0
@expect arm.grip_state[3] == 0
@expect arm.grip_held[3] == -1
@expect arm.pay_model[3] == 0
@expect arm.pay_state[4] == 0
@expect arm.pay_model[4] == 0
@expect arm.coll == 0
@expect arm.off_reason == 0
@expect max arm.hits2 == 0
@reject ^ERROR
